":0.568,"class":"signal","n":133,"first":1893,"last":2025,"intercept":-50.7036910457963,"slope":0.03000683526999316,"total":4.0},"snow_normal":8.7},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows","records":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","change":"Tulsa's nights warmed over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1986.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 54\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>54\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 62\u00b0F, and the record is 84\u00b0F (1910). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Tulsa's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Tulsa has set <strong>58 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 81 that chance alone would give, and <strong>79 record highs</strong>, close to the 81 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (60). Tulsa's all-time high is 115\u00b0F, on August 10, 1936.","t_chg":"Tulsa's nights warmed over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 120 complete years: Tulsa's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.24), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1906. Tulsa's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.08) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.70\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.29 to +1.12). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 5 of 12 months. Highs rose in none.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Tulsa's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.41 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 40.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 1973 (69.88 in); the driest, 1956 (23.24 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}